# ── H1: secrets (SECURITY_THREAT_MODEL_AND_PLAN.md) ──────────────────────────
# Four Google/Gemini API keys reached this repo's public history via committed
# .env files. `.env` alone did not cover variants like .env.local / .env.production.
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
client_secret*.json
*-service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
.secrets/

# ── L3: build/crash artifacts that must never be committed ───────────────────
# `chemdoodle.zip` (36K of HTML saved under a .zip name) and `bash.exe.stackdump`
# had both been sitting in the tree; the zip was even tracked. The risk is not the
# junk itself but that a stray `git add -A` sweeps up whatever else lands here.
*.stackdump
*.dmp
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
*.swp
*~
recycle/
